Bash(gh pr create --label sandcastle --title "refactor(ocale): migrate places wire code to by-domain layout" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary

Migrates the `places` Resource of `@bedrock/ocale` into the by-Domain
folder layout established by [ADR-022](docs/adr/022-by-domain-folder-layout-for-ocale.md).
Wire code for the `places` Resource spans two upstream URL prefixes, so
it lands in two Domain sub-trees:

- `cloud-v2` `update` Operation under `src/domains/cloud-v2/places/`
- legacy `/universes/v1/{universeId}/places/{placeId}/versions`
  `publish`/`save` Operation under `src/domains/place-publishing/places/`

`resources/places/` now contains only `client.ts`,
`client.example.spec.ts`, `index.ts`. The client binds publish/save and
update from their respective Domain sub-trees. Public surface, wire
requests, parsed shapes, and operation keys (`places.publishVersion`,
`places.update`) are preserved end-to-end; conformance and integration
tests pass without modification.

## Why

ADR-022 establishes the by-Domain layout to replace the peer-folder
Resource layout that does not scale to the full Open Cloud surface. The
universes/icon/thumbnails consolidation in #300 validated the
convention; this PR is the next per-Resource migration. Issue #301
covers the universes Resource on a parallel branch.

## Naming the legacy Domain folder

The publish/save Operation lives at the literal URL prefix
`/universes/v1/...`. Applying ADR-022's drop-`legacy-`-and-version rule
yields `universes`, which collides with `domains/cloud-v2/universes/`
(the per-shape sub-tree the universes Resource will land in). The PR
deviates from the literal-prefix mapping in this one case and uses
`place-publishing/`, the name Roblox's docs use for the conceptual
Feature served by this URL prefix (`/cloud/guides/usage-place-publishing.md`).

## Commits

1. `refactor(ocale): migrate places update wire code into domains/cloud-v2`
2. `refactor(ocale): migrate places publish wire code into domains/place-publishing`
3. `test(ocale): reuse shared place-body helper in parsers spec` (post-`/simplify` cleanup)

## Test plan

- [x] `pnpm gen:example-tests` regenerated (no diff)
- [x] `pnpm lint` clean
- [x] `pnpm typecheck` clean
- [x] `pnpm test` all green (1328 ocale + workspace tests pass)
- [x] `pnpm build` clean (publint reports no issues)
- [x] `pnpm lint:unused` (knip) clean
- [ ] `pnpm mutate:changed` — could not complete inside the sandcastle docker sandbox (Stryker tries to spawn `ps`, which is not installed in the image); CI will run it on a clean checkout
- [ ] CI verifies the same on a clean checkout

Closes #304.

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
EOF
